"before the form can be submitted. This blocks bots that do not run "
"JavaScript. Invisible for real users (about one second). Check to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/SettingsFieldset.php:241
msgid "Check mx records of the email domain"
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/SettingsFieldset.php:253
msgid "Tell the visitor when his message may be a false positive"
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/SettingsFieldset.php:254
msgid ""
"By default, a spam is classified silently and the visitor is thanked as "
"usual, so a bot does not learn that it was caught. When checked, a message "
"marked as spam only by a check that may be wrong (too fast, proof-of-work, "
"reputation of the ip…) shows that it was not transmitted, without the "
"reason, and invites to retry. Warning: a bot learns then that it failed, and "
"these checks are mainly on timing, so it may adapt by posting more slowly."
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/SettingsFieldset.php:266
msgid "Email to suggest to a visitor whose message may be a false positive"
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/SettingsFieldset.php:267
msgid ""
"Used only when the visitor is told that his message was not transmitted."
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/SettingsFieldset.php:279
msgid "Notify the admins of the messages that may be false positives"
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/SettingsFieldset.php:280
msgid ""
"A message marked as spam only by a check that may be wrong (too fast, proof-"
"of-work, reputation of the ip…) remains marked as spam, but the admins "
"receive it, with \"[Possible spam]\" and the reasons, and the visitor is "
"thanked as usual, so a bot learns nothing. It is never sent to the author of "
"a resource nor confirmed to the visitor. The spams detected by a reliable "
"check are never sent."
msgstr ""

